#![doc = include_str!("../docs/overview.md")]
// Property and argument values are cloned out of shared/locked state through the same
// generated code path regardless of their concrete type, so a value's type being `Copy`
// (e.g. an interface property declared as an integer or float) is incidental, not a sign
// the clone is wasteful.
#![allow(clippy::clone_on_copy)]
// Schema validation serializes a field through `&self.field` so the same generated code
// works whether the field's type is `Copy` or not; dropping the borrow would fail to
// compile for non-Copy fields (moving out of `&self`), so it can't be done per-callsite.
#![allow(clippy::needless_borrows_for_generic_args)]
// Property and channel types nest Arc/RwLockWatch/Option around whatever type the
// interface declares (e.g. an optional list of structs), so how deep that nesting gets
// is up to the interface definition, not something a fixed set of type aliases here
// could pre-empt.
#![allow(clippy::type_complexity)]
// Generated functions for methods, signals, and commands take one parameter per
// argument the interface declares, so their arity is set by the interface definition,
// not something the generator can bound in advance.
#![allow(clippy::too_many_arguments)]

/// Long-form guides for using this interface.
